#: {{synonyms|en|Thesaurus:nonsense}}
#: {{ux|en|I decided it was a bunch of '''malarkey''' and stopped reading about halfway through.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Thomas Aloysius Dorgan|authorlink=Tad Dorgan|newspaper={{w|The Capital Times}}|location=Madison, Wis.|publisher=Capital Times Co.|date=2 April 1934|page=6|issn=0749-4068|oclc=7351334|passage='''Malachy'''—You said it—I wouldn't trust a lawyer no further than I could throw a case of Scotch.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|magazine=The Commentator|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Payson Publishing Co.|year=1939|volume=6|page=45|column=2|oclc=4278333|passage=It's a lot of '''mallarky''' for mothers, sisters, and sweethearts to ask "Laddie, when you're far away will you think of me?" The answer is NO! The girls who teach the soldier boys are kept busy as a bee. It's the soldier boys who pay.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Lawrence Lariar|authorlink=Lawrence Lariar|author2=Erle Stanley Gardner|authorlink2=Erle Stanley Gardner|author3=Marjorie Alan|title=The Girl with the Frightened Eyes [by Lawrence Lariar]; The Case of the Half-wakened Wife [by Erle Stanley Gardner]; Dark Prophecy [by Marjorie Alan]|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Detective Book Club|year=1945|page=127|oclc=6186260|passage=She shrugged. "I've told you all I know." / "'''Mallarky'''. You haven't even begun to spill and you know it."}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Merrick Pratt|title=Administering the Protective Equipment Program|editor=Gerard J. Riley|magazine=Modern Sanitation: The Magazine of Sanitation Management and Plant Housekeeping|location=Easton, Pa.|publisher=Powell Magazines|month=July|year=1957|volume=9|issue=1|page=21|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=SEVPAAAAYAAJ&pg=RA6-PA21|oclc=977829725|passage=If I told you that we had launched the glove washing program without effort it would be purely '''malarkey'''. Right off the bat we had some squawks about dermatitis.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Margery Allingham|authorlink=Margery Allingham|chapter=The String Man|title={{w|Cargo of Eagles}}|location=London|publisher={{w|Chatto & Windus}}|year=1968|oclc=459739|location2=London|publisher2=[[w:Vintage Books|Vintage]]|year2=2016|page2=91|pageurl2=https://books.google.com/books?id=x4SKAwAAQBAJ&pg=PA91|isbn2=978-0-09-951328-5|passage='Smuggling,' she said. 'has a fine romantic ring about it—once aboard the lugger, you heave ho and all that kind of '''malarky'''. [...]'}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Robert Ormond Case|title=Trouble at Midas Creek|editor={{w|Ben Hibbs}}|magazine={{w|The Saturday Evening Post}}|location=Philadelphia, Pa.; London|publisher={{w|Curtis Publishing Company}}|date=19 October 1957|volume=230|issue=16|page=64|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=DtoeAQAAMAAJ&pg=RA6-PA64|column=1|issn=0048-9239|oclc=613316682|passage=Save that '''malarkey''' for those old fossils at Midas Creek! You're aiming at the pot. So am I. I'm in control, but you and your infernal luck could upset the applecart.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Donald E[dwin] Westlake|authorlink=Donald E. Westlake|chapter=23|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=UqLQBQAAQBAJ&pg=PT54|title=Why Me?|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Viking Press|Viking]]|year=1983|isbn=978-0-670-76569-0|location2=[New York, N.Y.]|publisher2=MysteriousPress.com/[[w:Open Road Integrated Media|Open Road]]|year2=2011|isbn2=978-90-499-8649-0|passage=But, Tony, this has got to stay within the Department. None of our FBIers or state troopers or all them other '''malarkeys''' get to hear a word of it.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Alan Moore|authorlink=Alan Moore|author2=[[w:David Lloyd (comics|David Lloyd]], illustrator|title=[[w:V for Vendetta|V for Vendetta: This Vicious Cabaret]]|editor={{w|Dez Skinn}}|magazine=[[w:Warrior (comics)|Warrior]]|location=London|publisher={{w|Quality Communications}}|month=August|year=1983|issue=12|pages=92–93|oclc=9181490|newversion=quoted in|2ndauthor=[[w:Lance Parkin|Lance Parkin]]|title2=Magic Words: The Extraordinary Life of Alan Moore|location2=London|publisher2=[[w:The Quarto Group|Aurum Press]]|year2=2013|page2=196|pageurl2=https://books.google.com/books?id=JqUYAgAAQBAJ&pg=PA196|isbn2=978-1-78131-077-9|passage=There's mischiefs and '''malarkies''' / But no queers, or yids, or darkies. / Within this bastard's carnival, / This vicious cabaret!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Stephen Lowe|authorlink=Stephen Lowe (playwright)|chapter=Moving Pictures|title=Moving Pictures: Four Plays|series=Methuen New Theatrescript|location=London; New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Methuen Publishing|Methuen]]|year=1985|page=7|isbn=978-0-413-58780-0|passage=But I'm not havin' this film '''mallarky'''. I'm takin' no memories wi' me.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Richard Barry|chapter=Budgeting|title=The Management of International Oil Operations|location=Tulsa, Ok.|publisher=[[w:PennWell|PennWell Books]]|year=1993|page=331|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=rg-9HQ9faFsC&pg=PA331|isbn=978-0-87814-400-6|passage=A company that makes a fetish of never exceeding the budget invites game-playing and other '''malarky'''. It is easy to forget the obvious: that it involves no skill to come in on time and under budget if the schedule and budget are generous enough.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Nick Hornby|authorlink=Nick Hornby|chapter=13|title=[[w:About a Boy (novel)|About a Boy]]|location=London|publisher=[[w:Victor Gollancz Ltd|Gollancz]]|year=1998|isbn=978-0-575-06159-0|chapter2=13|chapterurl2=https://books.google.com/books?id=bX4cfmLisJ8C&pg=PT82|title2=About a Boy|location2=New York, N.Y.|publisher2={{w|Riverhead Books}}|year2=1998|isbn2=978-1-101-14736-8|passage="No. She was going through a ''{{w|Kramer vs. Kramer}}'' kind of thing at the time. You know, a sort of I-want-to-find-out-who-I-am '''malarkey'''." / "And did she find out who she was?" / "Not really. I don't know if anyone really does, do they?"}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Jules Verne|authorlink=Jules Verne|chapter=5|chapterurl=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/20,000_Leagues_Under_the_Seas_(Walter)/Chapter_29|translator=Frederick Paul Walter|title=[[w:Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Sea|20,000 Leagues under the Seas: An Underwater Tour of the World]]|series=Project Gutenberg eBook|seriesvolume=#2488|publisher={{w|Project Gutenberg}}|month=January|year=2001|section=part 2|oclc=914175360|passage="An underwater tunnel!" he exclaimed. "A connection between two seas! Who ever heard of such '''malarkey'''!"}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Johnny Rich|chapter=The Application Process|editor=Ruth Bushi|title=The Push Guide to Choosing a University|edition=2nd|location=Cheltenham, Gloucestershire|publisher={{w|Nelson Thornes}}|year=2004|page=68|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=t4SWQk7vCskC&pg=PA68|isbn=978-0-7487-9027-2|passage=This book isn't about the application process itself&nbsp;– how best to complete your UCAS form, what the codes are for exam awarding bodies, what to say in interviews and all that '''mullarkey'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Liz Talley|title=Sweet Talking Man|series=Harlequin Superromance|location=Don Mills, Ont.|publisher={{w|Harlequin Enterprises}}|year=2015|page=337|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=LgWpBAAAQBAJ&pg=PA337|isbn=978-0-373-60896-6|passage=That's a bunch of '''malarkey''' piled on '''malarkey'''. I knew the minute I saw you there was something special about you, [...]}}

